      "writtenOn": "2022-07-25T07:53:07Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Please refer table 2.4.9 in npcx datasheet. Few gpios\u0027 power wells don\u0027t belong to the core domain power well, `VCC1`. For example, gpio46, 47, and the whole gpio5 module belong to `VHIF` power rail and it supports both 1.8V and 3.3V power wells. \n\nIf VHIF is connected to 1.8V, all 8 gpios have the same 1.8V push-pull/open-drain drive type and detection input buffer. No needs to configure them with \u0027GPIO_VOLTAGE_1P8\u0027 flag. But if VHIF is connected to 3.3V, only gpio50 has the capability to switch detection level from 3.3V to 1.8V. I will add comments to describe it.",
